A||||6||Alex2004||wiring amber light's on 84 f/b conversion w/o changing wiring harness.||||3||
Z||000000||Alex2004||03-31-2001||11:35 PM||||We did the fastback conversion on my 84 SE, and i could either have amber lights on w/o parking and brake light, or just have the red ones,so i chose red.  But i am really wanting to wire them up.  And i thought maybe somewhere where the turn/stop light's meet i could possible snip the turn signal wire and run a wire to the amber light's so they will come on only w/o turn, and the red ones wouldn't come on cept parking and brake.  So I took my console off last night, and the panel under the steering wheel, and i found the lt Blue wire and Drk blue wires for turning and green for stop and hazard.  So i traces the green wire to the computer and used the test light and it works, and then i found alot of lt blue wires, and tested them and non of them come on w/ either turn signal and i had a good ground.  But anyway, what i am tring to say is do any of you know here i could find where the stop/turn light wiring connect for the tail lights so the amber light's will work they do on normal fastbacks.  Please let me know if you have any ideas!!!!! Thanks...<P>Alex   <A HREF="mailto:abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Pontiaddict||04-01-2001||02:59 AM||||So, did you convince your dad to do what I told you to do in the chat room? If anyone else has to do this, just cut the white wire running from the brake switch and run it from the switch, to the back brake lights, where you will have to cut the old power wires (they would be the dark green and the yellow ones, the others are for the parking lights and the ground) and run the new wire to them. Cut the parking light wire going to the amber lights (I think it's brown but I'm not sure. But it's not the yellow, dark green, or black ones, so it would be what's left). Make sure what's left of the white wire (the end that runs into the turn signal flashers) is kept from shorting out, as well as the wires you cut from the lights.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Pontiaddict (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||04-01-2001||02:24 PM||||Hey,  I FIANLLY convinced my dad this morning when i told him about it, i had to explain it over and over, and then i unplugged the brake switch, and then he was like Oh, ok...  So i am going to run the wire today and go buy the light sockets from a "FIERO GUY" we know probably today, and hopfully i should have it done either today or tomorrow!!!  But thanks for all your help!!!  I'll let you all know how it turns out!<P>Alex....   <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Alex2004||04-01-2001||09:48 PM||||Well I rewired my brake light's and wired the amber lights and it works just like an 86 GT  Thanks for all your help!!!  And i am really glad i got it done!!!  Thanks!!!<P>Alex  <A HREF="mailto:abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||10
